# ACM Knowledge Database -- Auto-Update Protocol

**Location:** `/Users/ashafi/Documents/work/notes/knowledge/`

A unified knowledge database covering 14 ACM subsystems. Agents MUST update it when they learn verified new facts about ACM architecture, UI behavior, failure patterns, or health issues.

## When to Read (BEFORE acting on ACM-related tasks)

Before performing any ACM-related task, check if the knowledge DB has relevant content. Use `acm-knowledge` MCP with `search_knowledge(query=<task topic>)`. If the MCP is unavailable, read the relevant file directly from `/Users/ashafi/Documents/work/notes/knowledge/`.

| Task Type | Read These First |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Writing or updating test cases | `conventions/test-case-format.md`, `conventions/polarion-html-templates.md`, `ui/<area>.md` |
| Investigating cluster health | `diagnostics/diagnostic-layers.md`, `diagnostics/diagnostic-traps.md`, `health/<subsystem>/known-issues.md` |
| Writing automation scripts | `automation/playwright/<area>.md` or `automation/cypress/<area>.md` |
| Answering architecture questions | `architecture/<subsystem>/architecture.md`, `data-flow/<subsystem>/data-flow.md` |
| Classifying test failures | `failures/<subsystem>/failure-signatures.md`, `failures/classification-decision-tree.md` |
| Hunting for bugs | `failures/<subsystem>/failure-signatures.md`, `architecture/<subsystem>/architecture.md` |
| Verifying bug fixes | `failures/<subsystem>/failure-signatures.md`, `health/<subsystem>/known-issues.md` |
| Investigating or deep-diving a topic | `architecture/<subsystem>/architecture.md`, `data-flow/<subsystem>/data-flow.md`, `ui/<area>.md` |
| ACM cluster operations | `architecture/<subsystem>/architecture.md`, `baselines/` |

## When to Update (ALL conditions must be true)

1. The fact is **verified** -- confirmed via live cluster (`oc` output), official docs (`rhacm-docs/`), source code (acm-source MCP), or JIRA/Polarion
2. The fact is **not already present** -- read the target file first, check for duplicates
3. The fact is **relevant to ACM QE work** -- architecture, UI behavior, failure patterns, health diagnostics, testing considerations
4. The fact is **durable** -- not a temporary state (e.g., "bm12 is running ACM 2.16" is ephemeral; "ACM 2.16 introduced FG-RBAC" is durable)

## When NOT to Update

- Ephemeral cluster state (pod counts on a specific cluster, current build tags)
- Speculative or unverified information
- Information already covered in the target file (even if worded differently)
- Personal workflow notes (use Engram or `notes/` instead)

## Permission Exemption

Knowledge database updates are **exempt from the file-creation checkpoint** in `agent-safety.mdc`. The user has explicitly authorized automatic knowledge updates. No need to ask before writing to files under `notes/knowledge/`.

## Directory Map -- Where Each Fact Goes

| Fact Type | Target Directory | File Pattern | Frontmatter type | Example |
|-----------|-----------------|--------------|------------------|---------|
| How a subsystem works (components, CRDs, pods, controllers, reconciliation) | `architecture/<subsystem>/` | `architecture.md` | `architecture` | "The subscription-controller generates ManifestWork per target cluster" |
| How data flows through a subsystem | `data-flow/<subsystem>/` | `data-flow.md` | `data-flow` | "Search collector sends metadata to indexer via gRPC" |
| UI behavior (routes, translations, field orders, wizard steps, filtering) | `ui/` | `<area>.md` | `ui` | "Applications overview tab shows Subscription and ArgoCD apps" |
| Known health issues, bugs, degradation patterns | `health/<subsystem>/` | `known-issues.md` | `health` | "ACM-28668: Status sync re-emits events causing hub API throttling" |
| Failure signatures for test classification | `failures/<subsystem>/` | `failure-signatures.md` | `failures` | "Propagator TLS cert corruption causes all policy operations to fail" |
| Expected cluster state (pod counts, services, webhooks) | `baselines/` | Various `.yaml` | `baselines` | "search-postgres StatefulSet expects 1 replica" |
| Playwright test automation (fixtures, page objects, selectors, gotchas) | `automation/playwright/` | `<area>.md` | `automation` | "rbac-test.ts provides asUser(role) returning { page }" |
| Cypress test automation (views, actions, selectors, gotchas) | `automation/cypress/` | `<area>.md` | `automation` | "managedClustersSelectors exports cluster table locators" |

